class_name Laws
extends RefCounted
## The customs and laws a tribe can live under. Nobody scripts which ones a tribe takes: each year
## the ruler weighs what suits their own nature, what the strongest faction wants, what the times
## seem to call for (a famine, a war, dissent) and what the people's culture will bear. Laws pass,
## are blocked by a strong council, are repealed, or are swept away by a revolution. Emergency
## laws are meant to be temporary; proud and greedy rulers rarely give them back.
##
## law -> {
##   "name", "age" (the earliest age it can appear in), "tech" (needed, or ""),
##   "faction": who pushes for it (see Society.FACTIONS),
##   "traits": ruler trait -> how much it draws (+) or repels (-) them,
##   "when": situations that make it seem needed (see SocietySystem.situation()),
##   "culture": axis -> fit (+1 means a tribe high on that axis welcomes it, -1 that it resents it),
##   "push": axis -> yearly drift of the tribe's culture while it is in force,
##   "freedom", "control": added to the tribe's freedom and control,
##   "fear": the least fear the law keeps alive,
##   "power": faction -> power it grants,
##   "effects": mechanical effects, read with Society.effect() and Society.flag(),
##   "excludes": laws it can't stand beside,
##   "replaces": laws it takes the place of (they go when it passes, and can't return beside it),
##   "dystopian": it moves the tribe toward a darker destiny,
##   "description",
## }
## Effects that multiply (default 1): work, births, split, war, discovery, pollution, fights.
## Effects that add (default 0): tax, tithe, share, mood, faith, propaganda, surveillance,
## guards and officials (hands per person the law wants in those jobs).
## Flags (true when present): hereditary, class_marriage, birth_permits, bonded, detain, exile,
## elections, social_credit, emergency.
